        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks opened a route to unprecedented frequency standards and precision tests of fundamental physics. Their invention is a major experimental advance with broad scientific reach.",
        "attribution": "Katori and Ye developed complementary approaches that established the field; both have strong claims to original invention and realization.",
        "maturity": "Clock performance and applications have advanced over many years, with independent groups confirming the underlying methods.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The field has grown through major contributions from other groups, making the appropriate scope of the prize important."
        ]
      }
    },
