        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological insulators revealed a new organizing principle for electronic states and stimulated a broad, durable field of condensed matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele supplied foundational theory; Molenkamp's experiments established the predicted edge transport. The theory and its decisive experimental test are both essential.",
        "maturity": "The effect has been tested in multiple material systems, although isolating ideal transport signatures remains experimentally demanding.",
